{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509201-have-you-used-any-4th-generation-ancients-in-your-games","id":1509201,"title":"Have you used any 4th generation ancients in your games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-21T09:39:00-07:00","id":1509201,"title":"Have you used any 4th generation ancients in your games?","content":"This was based on the Sybil being depicted post and I wonder if you have used any direct childer of the antidulivans in your games? We personally haven't in our games with the lowest generation kindred being of the 8th and 9th generation, but there is some thought that a member of the 5th or 6th generation might appear in a game down the road. As it stands there is no plans of having a 4th generation member showing up at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T09:58:27-07:00","id":1509207,"title":"","content":"The closest we got to generation 4 was generation 6, and that one already took some work and one of them cost me two characters to my team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T10:04:34-07:00","id":1509209,"title":"","content":"I hope that you get two good new characters to your team soon.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T10:27:30-07:00","id":1509212,"title":"","content":"I would have thought everyone ran Chicago by Night back in the day. Or do you mean people using them as players?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T10:39:18-07:00","id":1509213,"title":"","content":"I ran one game with a mixed group of experienced players and new players, to keep things simple the group was attacked by a group of sabbat ghouls while they were out camping. The soon to be coterie managed to defeat the ghoul pack. This impressed a passing Gangrel and so she embraced them, gave them the &quot;welcome to the unlife club&quot; speech and left them to figure the rest out.<br /> <br /> The group had several smaller adventures, but eventually they got into a situation where the local prince wanted to know more about them, Ventrue get bent out of shape when their Dominate doesn't work at an embarrassing moment. The local Tremere checked their Generation and promptly ran screaming out of the meeting room. All the PCs were 4th generation and had 9 dots in Fortitude, needless to say the newer players enjoyed the power trip, while the experienced players went somewhat pale when they realized the situation their coterie was now in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T17:32:49-07:00","id":1509241,"title":"","content":"I don't prefer any childer of the Antedeluvians to be active. Any still existing would be in torpor, though that state could still allow them to affect the game world. I don't want anyone (PC or NPC) to be able to speak to someone who has direct knowledge of the Antedeluvians. I want there to be a buffer (however theoretical) to keep the nature of the Antedeluvians a mystery.<br /> <br /> I would allow someone to be of the 4th generation who obtained their position that way by diablerie. Mithras would be an example in my chronicles. However, I more or less only have characters who are fifth generation or later in chronicles.<br /> <br /> This does mean I downgrade various canonical characters who are said to be 4th generation in my chronicles. Menele and Helena are 5th generation as a result, and therefore every vampire of their line also gets downgraded by a generation. I haven't found that to be any meaningful change. It also impacts other characters like Kemintiri, though since in my chronicles I distinguish two &quot;Sets&quot; (the actual Antedeluvian and his 4th generation childe who is the brother of Osiris), I can still use her by simply making her the childe of the 4th generation one.<br /> <br /> In terms of actual play, this has very little practical effect. I try to limit NPCs in a city to 7th generation - just enough to allow players to have an 8th generation character. I limit characters of 5th or 6th generation to special cities (like Chicago) or characters who are only visiting or in correspondence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T22:33:54-07:00","id":1509253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509201-have-you-used-any-4th-generation-ancients-in-your-games?p=1509209#post1509209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope that you get two good new characters to your team soon.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That was years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T22:46:39-07:00","id":1509254,"title":"","content":"I am running a Chicago by Night with Menelao and Helena. I haven't decided yet, and it's very unlikely to even turn up I'm the game whether Menelao's Sire was actually Troile or he got to 4th generation through Diablerie, but I've definitely turned his &quot;badguyness&quot; up to leave that option open.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T08:01:41-07:00","id":1509719,"title":"","content":"Yes, at least twice.<br /> <br /> Plot summaries follow:<br /> <br /> <b>Minor:</b> In this game we were high ranking Ancillae attach\u00e9s to a Prince, and were taking part in a conclave. When the subject of the induction of a large contingent of the Clan of Shadows came up, most of the conclave didn't quite trust the lasombra <i>&quot;fleeing&quot;</i> the sabbat to stick to the Traditions, and after a few speakers came to the stage to defend their position semi-publically (all stepping out of the shadows and doing various cool abyssal themed actions) a man politely entered through the doors, walked up to the stage. And <i>every single lasombra shut the hell up</i>. He then, in a deep clear voice, set the terms of them joining (I don't remember, but they involved some concessions of controlled territory as well as prisoners of war so to speak) and giving his personal guarantee that <i>his people</i> will comport themselves properly. No one actually asked his name, but after the chat, we asked the Prince who he was and, in very low tones, she said that his name was Montano, Child of Lasombra. Which I kinda liked because it demonstrated what the elders might require as proof before moving their allegiances a bit.<br /> <br /> <b>Major </b>(Forgive me for adding a bit of dramatic flair, I don't recall all the details and had to fill some in)<b>:</b> In a game of Nodists who, after some investigation, had some pretty good evidence that a Malkavian Methuselah slept under Jerusalem (Yeah, <u><b>I know</b></u>, but <b>the <u>players</u> did <u>not</u></b>). They wanted to find the methuselah for various reasons, from examining his burial ground, to diablerie. One of them, Thomas, was a dominate malkavian for whom the Great Prank didn't <i>lift</i> and instead broke him further (an extra permanent derangement). After a long time of trying to triangulate his location by mapping the <i>waves</i> of madness (effectively statistics based on mental disorder frequency by area) and a lot of backroom deals with the Ashirra, they managed to find a trail.<br /> <br /> They came upon an empty house with an opening into an old cave. There they discovered where the madness was coming from - a woman with a very very convincingly painted 3rd eye, was running a makeshift hospice - and in said hospice she was taking care of a <b>lot</b> of the Gnawed (Gnawed are malkavians who were completely broken by the embrace - think terribly disabling madness). One of them (the Tremere) used thaumaturgy and auspex to determine that the resonance of all those combined tended to leak. Thomas was completely debilitated by the echoes of the network here and started heavily hallucinating. The woman with the third eye who went by the name Atarah was a very helpful if slightly mad (through proximity) elder. She did offer each a gift if they promised not to tell anyone of her shelter, and the gifts were somewhat satisfactory - a tale leading them to further knowledge, a bit of occult lore (think blood magic instruction), some recollections from other noddist fragments. Cool enough but also slightly disappointing. Thomas just asked for help with his hallucinations (something poetic like, bring me closer to the truth - I remember it fit like hell with the plot so I went with it) - so she took him to another patient of hers, one of the broken ones, and she did some kind of healing ritual on both. His hallucinations seemed to clear and he was sent on his way.<br /> <br /> Taking the way up I started describing inconsistencies. The climb was a bit more difficult than it should've been, the house looked too dusty, like they took too long in there, the city seemed quite empty; and after passing through two narrow streets, they see light before them fold like a mirage and they find themselves exiting a large temple carved in the side of a Canyon. Completely confused, finding themselves suddenly low on blood (all except Thomas, who seems to have somehow filled up) and doubting their senses, they encounter a small group of tourists being shown around the place by a man dressed like a Bedouin. Some inquire as to where they are, Thomas just starts spouting Atarah's name. I tell him that every time he says the name, he feels like something is <b>very </b>wrong. They learn that they are in <a href=\"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/69e2cf60-ad59-4d20-bdd1-dc96f40ab4e8/petra-world-heritage-jordan.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Petra</a>. Thomas starts seeing peculiar flashbacks disagreeing with his recent memories. He sees them go into a house, yes, but then he gets images of them offering blood to a hungry <i>wall</i> and the earth opening up and swallowing them, dark tunnels - in general weird shit. And now they seem to be about 250 km away from where they started. Looking back at Atarah, he recalls another disturbing detail - all the patients, all the gnawed were men, and they all had the same face. It's at that point that a tourist hears him say her name and just offhand wonders why the crazy man keeps mumbling Crown (Yeah, this part was cheesy but I couldn't resist).<br /> <br /> AAAnd at that point the scales fall from our poor malkavian and he remembers. He remembers when the methuselah fell on them, when she fed from each - he remembers her talking to a man that <b>wasn't</b> there but they could see him - or aspects of him, all over <i>his tomb</i>. And he remembers when he asked her to bring him closer to the Truth, where she told him that most of them were lost and her Father needed a refuge - she was too small, too alone, so Thomas would have to bear the burden as well, and through Him, see the Truth. And she knelt next to him, and tore her hair from her head, and wove a crown from it, putting it on his head, anointing him with her blood. And he screamed. And the madness flowed out of him, and into the people and his coterie - and they fed on the mortals and the mortals tore each other to pieces. And the flowed through him in that act, and the Great Prank was lifted, and he could finally <i>see</i> see the network as it was - the many faced madman that danced through their minds.<br /> <br /> And that's how Thomas, the newest Coronatus, was re-born, adopted child of the Plague Bride, one of the keepers of Malkav's slightly dented psyche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12911-lateral-psychotropy","name":"Lateral.Psychotropy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T09:17:13-07:00","id":1509734,"title":"","content":"In my games it often happens that the player characters meet or at least hear from the 4th generation vampires who usually pull the strings of many events in the game. I just need to be clear that 90% of my games in the last 20+ years were set in the Dark Ages, so it's much more common to meet/hear about Cainites of the 5th and 4th generation, most of the important cities in this era are run by vampires of these generations. Rarely though do the players face them as opponents and when they do, &quot;weird things&quot; tend to happen (and TPK is the likelier scenario if they press to fight such beasts).<br /> <br /> I like to keep the mystery, of course, but they rarely meet these Demi-gods personally in the game and when they do, it's just a glimpse and they don't normally have the chance to figure out much about these Cainites. Then again I have ST countless games in this span of time (20+ years) and once I made an Elder chronicle (if I'm not mistaken it was around 2004). Using Elysium as a basis for rules, but I set the game in the early Middle Ages and I had players of the 5th generation, still, even in these games, the gap between 5th and 4th in my games is usually a big one and in this elder chronicle the PCs didn't last long, as well as the story itself, because they got destroyed in a cataclysmic battle near Constantinople.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T09:20:53-07:00","id":1509736,"title":"","content":"In other words, I don't keep my players &quot;grounded&quot; at higher generations (and in Dark Ages one can be expected to start the game as a 7th generation per the rules), if the story allows them to lower their generation, it's ok, I'm more than used to deal with such things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T11:24:41-07:00","id":1509752,"title":"","content":"Sometimes I'll play a mental game where one of the factions is ultimatly under acting on the agency of an ancient. Usually they'll get a cameo","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T15:23:03-07:00","id":1510421,"title":"","content":"I follow canon in having Mithras active in the British Isles during the Dark Ages period.<br /> <br /> Regarding my own characters, no, I don't have any active members of the 4th generation. For my Dark Ages setting, I have one 4th generation Gangrel in torpor under Silbury Hill, exerting limited influence telepathically, and her childe, who is active but posing as a neonate and staying out of politics. Other than that, I have three 6th generation, three 7th, and all others 8th or below. The two eldest characters were Embraced c. 600 and 300 BC, there are four ancient Romans (first century or later), and the others date from the the dark ages and afterwards.<br /> <br /> For my V5 setting there is one 7th generation character born in 106 AD, a smattering of medieval holdouts of the 8th-11th generation, and all others born in the 17th century and afterwards. <br /> <br /> By and large, I don't like characters whose stat block is a big &quot;you ******* lose&quot;, which is one of the things I like about V5 - the power differential is less extreme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T20:55:43-07:00","id":1510463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JezMiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509201-have-you-used-any-4th-generation-ancients-in-your-games?p=1510421#post1510421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I follow canon in having Mithras active in the British Isles during the Dark Ages period.<br /> <br /> Regarding my own characters, no, I don't have any active members of the 4th generation. For my Dark Ages setting, I have one 4th generation Gangrel in torpor under Silbury Hill, exerting limited influence telepathically, and her childe, who is active but posing as a neonate and staying out of politics. Other than that, I have three 6th generation, three 7th, and all others 8th or below. The two eldest characters were Embraced c. 600 and 300 BC, there are four ancient Romans (first century or later), and the others date from the the dark ages and afterwards.<br /> <br /> For my V5 setting there is one 7th generation character born in 106 AD, a smattering of medieval holdouts of the 8th-11th generation, and all others born in the 17th century and afterwards.<br /> <br /> By and large, I don't like characters whose stat block is a big &quot;you ******* lose&quot;, which is one of the things I like about V5 - the power differential is less extreme.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly why I hate V5, this &quot;big you ******lose&quot; is very important to the atmosphere of &quot;cosmic horror&quot; that I feel is necessary for a vampire game( and hals always been there since the beginning). As any writing advice article you find out there, you're going to read that the story is as good as the antagonist, and he should ALWAYS pose a threat to the entire group, one of the reasons that made me start as a ST weeks after I started playing the game some 2 decades and half ago is that I saw many of my inexperienced friends who made antagonists who were basically a joke, that is the number one mistake you make in any story. Make the antagonists scary, absurdly so if necessary, never let there be any doubt about its powers and capacity to absolutely obliterate the entire group. Without the threat of a powerful antagonist, it's very hard to write a good story. The group should always be afraid in a WoD game. It's not D&amp;D.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T01:01:50-07:00","id":1510472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509201-have-you-used-any-4th-generation-ancients-in-your-games?p=1510463#post1510463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's exactly why I hate V5, this &quot;big you ******lose&quot; is very important to the atmosphere of &quot;cosmic horror&quot; that I feel is necessary for a vampire game( and hals always been there since the beginning). As any writing advice article you find out there, you're going to read that the story is as good as the antagonist, and he should ALWAYS pose a threat to the entire group, one of the reasons that made me start as a ST weeks after I started playing the game some 2 decades and half ago is that I saw many of my inexperienced friends who made antagonists who were basically a joke, that is the number one mistake you make in any story. Make the antagonists scary, absurdly so if necessary, never let there be any doubt about its powers and capacity to absolutely obliterate the entire group. Without the threat of a powerful antagonist, it's very hard to write a good story. The group should always be afraid in a WoD game. It's not D&amp;D.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Chacun \u00e0 son go\u00fbt</i>. Anything that you and your players enjoy is right for you.<br /> <br /> My own perspective is that while it's not D&amp;D, it's not Call of Cthulhu either. It's billed as a game of personal horror, not cosmic horror. And an antagonist can be scary without being able to physically stomp on an entire coterie at once. Hannibal Lector didn't have superpowers. Nor did Lord Vetinari. Both were credible antagonists.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T08:43:27-07:00","id":1510492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Chacun \u00e0 son go\u00fbt</i>.\u200b </div> </div> </div>I absolutely agree with you there, I just expressed my opinion, that's why I said &quot;I hate&quot;, I think that each game is different, and I didn't mean to say that &quot;only my vision of the game is right&quot; or anything similar (I've always hated this stance).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My own perspective is that while it's not D&amp;D, it's not Call of Cthulhu either. It's billed as a game of personal horror, not cosmic horror. </div> </div> </div>I understand, but what I meant is that while it's surely a game of &quot;personal horror&quot;, these elements of &quot;ancients beings being out there, waiting for the moment to devour you all&quot; was always there, since the beginning, so in my opinion it's something that V5 in a way (not totally I believe) got rid of, and it's a reason for many complaints from veteran players, etc. Again, this is my vision of the game coupled with the elements the game gave us since the beginning of the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And an antagonist can be scary without being able to physically stomp on an entire coterie at once. Hannibal Lector didn't have superpowers. Nor did Lord Vetinari. Both were credible antagonists. </div> </div> </div>Surely, but they were damn scary and made everyone feel scared about their actions and potential actions, etc (not to mention some elements or &quot;coincidence or pure luck&quot; that made it look like they many times had the upper hand when dealing with the protagonists, that in a tabletop RPG are much easier to evoke through the use of powers). I didn't mean that the antagonist <b>must</b> be able to necessarily physically stomp the entire coterie, especially because the antagonist in any case, could be even an organization, more than one character, or simply a character who has so much political power that you never have the chance to be face to face with him to &quot;beat him into submission&quot; even when you'd be able to.<br /> There are certainly many ways to create a good story (and a good antagonist), I just pointed out what I think about the setting, again, <b>my opinion</b>. I think mystery and horror are especially important to make an interesting WoD story and both were elements present since the start of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}